# L §5.18 example ask q1, copied: "values, one line per binding tuple ..., the expressions in the order written";
# "Lines are ordered by binding tuple in binding order" (here families is an index of two keys and months the
# built-in index of a two-month run).  payable is the §5.11 def's base rule, max(0 PLN, entitled − excess).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-11-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index families = [f1, f2]

input entitled[f in families, m in months]: money PLN
input excess[f in families, m in months]: money PLN

def payable[f in families, m in months]: money PLN at start_of(m)
  rule base = max(0 PLN, entitled[f, m] - excess[f, m])

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  entitled[f1, *] = 500.00 PLN
  entitled[f2, *] = 50.00 PLN
  excess[*, *] = 100.00 PLN

ask q1: payable[f, m] for f in families, m in months law 2026-12-31
=== expect
q1 (f = f1, m = 2026-11): 400.00 PLN
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-12-31
q1 (f = f1, m = 2026-12): 400.00 PLN
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-12-31
q1 (f = f2, m = 2026-11): 0.00 PLN
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-12-31
q1 (f = f2, m = 2026-12): 0.00 PLN
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-12-31
